v0.096: Print Agent system tray app with Settings GUI; add Setup Guide to docs/

- Print Agent now runs as a system tray icon (printer with a person behind
  it) instead of a bare console window. Right-click for Settings (set the
  SumatraPDF.exe path from a GUI, persisted to %APPDATA%\BNSPrintAgent\
  config.json - no more editing files/env vars) and Exit.
- Added print-agent/build_exe.bat + requirements.txt to build a standalone
  BNSPrintAgent.exe via PyInstaller (bundles the tray icon, no Python
  needed on the PC that runs it). Running "python agent.py" directly still
  works exactly as before, tray icon included when pystray/Pillow are
  installed, falling back to plain console mode otherwise.
- Added print-agent/generate_icon.py + assets/icon.ico (procedurally drawn,
  no external asset).
- Folded the standalone Setup Guide PDF into docs/BNS_Warehouse_Setup_Guide.pdf
  as planned, updated its Print Agent section for the new tray/exe workflow,
  and listed it in README's docs/ section.

